        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Announcing DPoP Support for Google OAuth: Securing Refresh Tokens]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[Google OAuth Platform now supports DPoP (Demonstrating Proof-of-Possession) to sender-constrain refresh tokens, neutralizing Infostealer malware and adversary-in-the-middle attacks. By cryptographically binding long-lived refresh tokens while maintaining short-lived access tokens as standard Bearer tokens, developers achieve robust credential security without incurring high-QPS API performance overhead. Additionally, developers integrating multi-agent or Model Context Protocol (MCP) workloads can use Google Cloud Secure Token Service (STS) to handle secure token delegation across agent chains.]]></description>
            <link>https://developers.googleblog.com/announcing-dpop-support-for-google-oauth-securing-refresh-tokens/</link>
            <guid isPermaLink="false">https://developers.googleblog.com/announcing-dpop-support-for-google-oauth-securing-refresh-tokens/</guid>
            <pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2020 09:22:00 GMT</pubDate>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Announcing MCP support in Apigee hybrid: agentic tools that run in your own cluster]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[Apigee hybrid 1.17.0 introduces native Model Context Protocol (MCP) support, enabling the MCP data plane to run directly within your own Kubernetes cluster. This architecture ensures that AI agent request traffic and tool execution remain entirely inside your infrastructure while pulling configuration updates from the control plane. Developers can expose OpenAPI 3.0.x specifications as discoverable MCP tools, leverage existing security policies and API products, and trace end-to-end requests using W3C trace context headers.]]></description>
            <link>https://developers.googleblog.com/announcing-mcp-support-in-apigee-hybrid-agentic-tools-that-run-in-your-own-cluster/</link>
            <guid isPermaLink="false">https://developers.googleblog.com/announcing-mcp-support-in-apigee-hybrid-agentic-tools-that-run-in-your-own-cluster/</guid>
            <pubDate>Sun, 21 Jun 2020 03:22:00 GMT</pubDate>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Gemini 4 Argon for Robotics]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[Gemini 4 Argon is a general-purpose physical reasoning model designed to enhance workflows across the robotics stack with advanced capabilities in physical understanding, code generation, and visual-semantic reasoning. Developers can access and integrate Argon across Google's developer platforms—including Google AI Studio, the Gemini API, and Google Antigravity—to build and test sophisticated robotic applications. By leveraging simulation tools like MuJoCo and code-as-policies, engineers can seamlessly transition from real-world data or sketches to physically verified robot control and self-improvement workflows.]]></description>
            <link>https://developers.googleblog.com/gemini-4-argon-for-robotics/</link>
            <guid isPermaLink="false">https://developers.googleblog.com/gemini-4-argon-for-robotics/</guid>
            <pubDate>Thu, 18 Jun 2020 11:42:00 GMT</pubDate>
        </item>
